925
00:39:03.280 --> 00:39:06.780
He also said that it was very challenging spatially.

926
00:39:07.200 --> 00:39:11.760
He said for him, it was like the flip side of the coin to Diversity Day.

927
00:39:12.180 --> 00:39:17.320
Diversity Day, it was like, how do I do this whole episode confined in this small room?

928
00:39:17.320 --> 00:39:22.920
And then this episode was, how do I do this episode and establish relationships and intimacy

929
00:39:22.920 --> 00:39:25.400
in a huge wide parking lot?

930
00:39:25.780 --> 00:39:30.440
He said when he directs, he's always trying to find those relationship moments.

931
00:39:30.440 --> 00:39:34.300
He's always trying to find the family, to establish family.

932
00:39:34.560 --> 00:39:35.280
I love that.

933
00:39:35.400 --> 00:39:36.200
I did, too.

934
00:39:36.320 --> 00:39:39.900
But it's really challenging when people are very spread apart.

935
00:39:39.900 --> 00:39:41.920
So I just love that.

936
00:39:42.080 --> 00:39:47.360
But, yeah, we talked a good bit of our phone conversation was just about how hot it was.

937
00:39:47.560 --> 00:39:50.460
And he said, in the end, I was glad no one collapsed.

