00:42:40.980 --> 00:42:44.240
Well, I really loved Dwight's pick so much.

985
00:42:44.240 --> 00:42:46.080
I feel like we need to hear it.

986
00:42:47.260 --> 00:42:47.540
Fine.

987
00:42:48.300 --> 00:42:49.680
Physician's desk reference.

988
00:42:49.940 --> 00:42:50.360
Nice.

989
00:42:50.540 --> 00:42:50.660
Smart.

990
00:42:51.000 --> 00:42:51.620
Hollowed out.

991
00:42:51.840 --> 00:42:59.960
Inside, waterproof matches, iodine tablets, beet seeds, protein bars, NASA blanket, and

992
00:42:59.960 --> 00:43:03.720
in case I get bored, Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's Stone.

993
00:43:04.220 --> 00:43:06.520
No, Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban.

994
00:43:06.880 --> 00:43:07.360
Question.

995
00:43:07.660 --> 00:43:09.500
Did my shoes come off in the plane crash?

996
00:43:10.240 --> 00:43:10.680
Amazing.

997
00:43:11.100 --> 00:43:11.500
Amazing.

998
00:43:11.740 --> 00:43:12.740
He's speaking to me.

999
00:43:13.060 --> 00:43:14.180
I know he is.

1000
00:43:14.360 --> 00:43:15.520
Physician's desk reference.

1001
00:43:15.920 --> 00:43:16.840
Such a smart answer.

1002
00:43:17.020 --> 00:43:18.200
I wouldn't hollow it out.

1003
00:43:18.380 --> 00:43:19.840
I wouldn't hollow it out either.

1004
00:43:20.460 --> 00:43:23.740
But, you know, the scene is a little bit longer in the superfan episode.

1005
00:43:24.060 --> 00:43:28.740
Right after Dwight says, did my shoes come off in the plane crash, he goes on to say,

1006
00:43:29.040 --> 00:43:29.960
this is important.

1007
00:43:30.360 --> 00:43:31.500
Leather is a food source.

1008
00:43:31.900 --> 00:43:35.860
Leather from shoes can be boiled down to a simple broth that can sustain a man for over

1009
00:43:35.860 --> 00:43:36.580
two weeks.

1010
00:43:37.600 --> 00:43:38.900
Well, lady, I had to know.

1011
00:43:39.520 --> 00:43:42.220
Is this one of those things that Dwight is half right about?

1012
00:43:42.520 --> 00:43:43.320
Oh, my God.

1013
00:43:43.520 --> 00:43:44.100
Tell me.

1014
00:43:44.260 --> 00:43:44.920
I need to know.

1015
00:43:45.120 --> 00:43:45.360
Okay.

1016
00:43:45.360 --> 00:43:47.820
For my survivalist brain needs to know the answer.

1017
00:43:47.960 --> 00:43:51.140
Can I drink the broth of my boiled shoe?

1018
00:43:51.560 --> 00:43:52.020
Well?

1019
00:43:52.020 --> 00:43:53.380
Will it sustain me?

1020
00:43:53.560 --> 00:43:54.560
Well, here's the thing, lady.

1021
00:43:54.920 --> 00:43:56.420
The quick answer is no.

1022
00:43:56.880 --> 00:43:58.940
You should not eat leather from shoes.

1023
00:43:59.100 --> 00:44:03.680
Because while technically leather contains some protein, most commercially tanned leather

1024
00:44:03.680 --> 00:44:08.280
used in shoes is treated with chemicals and dyes, making it unsafe to consume, and

1025
00:44:08.280 --> 00:44:10.180
eating it can cause digestive issues.

1026
00:44:10.340 --> 00:44:10.480
Sure.

1027
00:44:10.480 --> 00:44:11.260
You're eating it raw.

1028
00:44:11.440 --> 00:44:12.380
Eating it raw, yes.

1029
00:44:12.500 --> 00:44:13.640
But what if I boil it?

1030
00:44:13.820 --> 00:44:16.100
It's still going to be boiled in its chemicals.

1031
00:44:16.400 --> 00:44:17.440
I guess that's true.

1032
00:44:17.740 --> 00:44:18.060
Don't we?

1033
00:44:18.320 --> 00:44:22.760
Remember in like old cartoons, you would see the cartoon characters boil their shoe?

1034
00:44:22.920 --> 00:44:24.860
Well, here's what I was going to say about that.

1035
00:44:25.200 --> 00:44:27.760
There is this lore of eating your shoes.

1036
00:44:27.760 --> 00:44:29.080
It's been around a long time.

1037
00:44:29.080 --> 00:44:34.340
It's been shared in ledgers over history in extreme starvation situations.

1038
00:44:34.700 --> 00:44:40.320
For example, Sir John Franklin was a British Royal Navy officer and explorer.

1039
00:44:40.700 --> 00:44:46.680
And in his ledger from his ship between 1819 and 1822, things were not going well.

1040
00:44:46.840 --> 00:44:48.500
He was losing his crew to starvation.

1041
00:44:48.820 --> 00:44:52.560
And the survivors even attempted to eat their own leather boots.

1042
00:44:52.740 --> 00:44:56.360
And this is what gained Franklin the nickname of the man who ate his boots.

1043
00:44:56.820 --> 00:44:57.680
And he survived.

